{"success": true, "message": "Test details sent successfully", "data": {"test": {"_id": "69de21ec7e39d99b57bc5ac4", "analysisVideoCdn": "yt", "exam": ["605dfcb2f226ac25a8bd5fef"], "ctype": null, "position": 0, "order": 12, "enableCalculator": false, "isContinuousQuestion": false, "reattemptAvailable": false, "singleSectionMultipleSubjects": false, "timeRestricted": false, "title": "Thermodynamics - Test 4", "description": "Previous Year Questions as Chapter Test", "syllabus": "This test contains questions from all topics of this chapter included in the JEE Main syllabus. It includes a mix of questions from PYQs of JEE Main 2019 - 2025.", "totalTime": 50, "totalQuestions": 25, "totalMarks": 100, "bonusQuestions": null, "bonusMarks": null, "startDate": "2026-04-15T03:30:00.000Z", "endDate": "2027-04-30T00:00:00.000Z", "type": "free", "class": "605df635a37b7025c438d685", "instruction": "608289ffb160b022e9442c83", "subjects": [{"subjectId": "607018ee404ae53194e73d90", "totalMarks": 100, "bonusMarks": 0, "totalQuestions": 25, "bonusQuestions": 0, "_id": "69de4f142ee0e063d9235137"}], "sections": [{"sectionId": {"_id": "69de4f142ee0e063d92350e9", "title": "Physics Single Correct", "sectionType": "normal", "subject": "607018ee404ae53194e73d90", "questions": [{"_id": "69de4f142ee0e063d9235082", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60e08408faa0944a2c3d490b"], "topics": ["60c9e88cea076dc381c0e121"], "concepts": ["6117b88f67dbe2603c3e808d"], "question": {"text": "A diatomic gas <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>)</mo></math> does <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>200</mn><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi></math> of work when it is expanded isobarically. The heat given to the gas in the process is :"}, "options": [{"id": "205fa6", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>850</mn><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f142ee0e063d9235083"}, {"id": "c976bd", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>800</mn><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f142ee0e063d9235084"}, {"id": "c5f67d", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>600</mn><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f142ee0e063d9235085"}, {"id": "8d5ba9", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>700</mn><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f142ee0e063d9235086"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f142ee0e063d9235087", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60e08408faa0944a2c3d490b"], "topics": ["60c9e88cea076dc381c0e121"], "concepts": ["60e2fb5666f9ce3f243b4f09"], "question": {"text": "In an adiabatic process, which of the following statements is true?"}, "options": [{"id": "2e5b03", "text": "The molar heat capacity is infinite", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f142ee0e063d9235088"}, {"id": "0d316f", "text": "Work done by the gas equals the increase in internal energy", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f142ee0e063d9235089"}, {"id": "23c88d", "text": "The molar heat capacity is zero", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f142ee0e063d923508a"}, {"id": "fad7de", "text": "The internal energy of the gas decreases as the temperature increases", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f142ee0e063d923508b"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f142ee0e063d923508c", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60e08408faa0944a2c3d490b"], "topics": ["60c9e88cea076dc381c0e121"], "concepts": ["60c9e88bea076dc381c0e0f1"], "question": {"text": "<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>n</mi></math>&nbsp;mole of a perfect gas undergoes a cyclic process <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi><mi>C</mi><mi>A</mi></math>&nbsp;(see figure) consisting of the following processes.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo><mi>B</mi><mo>:</mo></math> Isothermal expansion at temperature <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>T</mi></math> so that the volume is doubled from <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>V</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math> to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>V</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><msub><mi>V</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math> and pressure changes from <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math> to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo><mi>C</mi><mo>:</mo></math> Isobaric compression at pressure <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math> to initial volume <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>V</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>.</mo></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>C</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>:</mo></math>&nbsp;Isochoric change leading to change of pressure from <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math> to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math></p><p>Total work done in the complete cycle <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi><mi>C</mi><mi>A</mi></math> is:</p><p><img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2F89ffb312-e807-4ae0-b59d-be6dac55c474-image.png?alt=media\" style=\"width: 270px; height: 222px;\" /></p>"}, "options": [{"id": "5fc459", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>n</mi><mi>R</mi><mi>T</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi>ln</mi><mn>2</mn><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow></mfenced></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f142ee0e063d923508d"}, {"id": "dcd564", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>n</mi><mi>R</mi><mi>T</mi><mi>ln</mi><mn>2</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f142ee0e063d923508e"}, {"id": "52a934", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>n</mi><mi>R</mi><mi>T</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi>ln</mi><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow></mfenced></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f142ee0e063d923508f"}, {"id": "1c4d78", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f142ee0e063d9235090"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f142ee0e063d9235091", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60e08408faa0944a2c3d490b"], "topics": ["60c9e88cea076dc381c0e121"], "concepts": ["6117bc0067dbe2603c3ec296"], "question": {"text": "A bicycle tyre is filled with air having pressure of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>270</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>kPa</mi></math>&nbsp;at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>27</mn><mo>&#176;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math>. The approximate pressure of the air in the tyre when the temperature increases to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>36</mn><mo>&#176;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math> is"}, "options": [{"id": "aaa0d2", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>270</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>kPa</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f142ee0e063d9235092"}, {"id": "7608eb", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>262</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>kPa</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f142ee0e063d9235093"}, {"id": "4487ae", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>278</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>kPa</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f142ee0e063d9235094"}, {"id": "91c4b5", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>360</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>kPa</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f142ee0e063d9235095"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f142ee0e063d9235096", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60e08408faa0944a2c3d490b"], "topics": ["60c9e88cea076dc381c0e121"], "concepts": ["60e567ab499d1e49588f95c7"], "question": {"text": "In a process, temperature and volume of one mole of an ideal monoatomic gas are varied according to the relation $\\mathrm{VT}=\\mathrm{K},$ where $\\mathrm{K}$ is a constant. In this process the temperature of the gas is increased by $\\Delta \\mathrm{T}$. The amount of heat absorbed by gas is (R is gas constant):"}, "options": [{"id": "b1c8c7", "text": "$\\frac{1}{2} \\mathrm{R} \\Delta \\mathrm{T}$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f142ee0e063d9235097"}, {"id": "86737b", "text": "$\\frac{1}{2} \\mathrm{KR} \\Delta \\mathrm{T}$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f142ee0e063d9235098"}, {"id": "c15ebb", "text": "$\\frac{3}{2} \\mathrm{R} \\Delta \\mathrm{T}$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f142ee0e063d9235099"}, {"id": "a145bf", "text": "$\\frac{2 \\mathrm{~K}}{3} \\Delta \\mathrm{T}$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f142ee0e063d923509a"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f142ee0e063d923509b", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60e08408faa0944a2c3d490b"], "topics": ["60c9e88cea076dc381c0e121"], "concepts": ["60e2fb5666f9ce3f243b4f09"], "question": {"text": "A monoatomic gas at pressure <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi></math> and volume <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>V</mi></math> is suddenly compressed to one eighth of its original volume. The final pressure at constant entropy will be"}, "options": [{"id": "dc933a", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f142ee0e063d923509c"}, {"id": "be4ddf", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>8</mn><mi>P</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f142ee0e063d923509d"}, {"id": "7f43c0", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>32</mn><mi>P</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f142ee0e063d923509e"}, {"id": "23d797", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>64</mn><mi>P</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f142ee0e063d923509f"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f142ee0e063d92350a0", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60e08408faa0944a2c3d490b"], "topics": ["60c9e88cea076dc381c0e121"], "concepts": ["6117b88f67dbe2603c3e808d"], "question": {"text": "Match List-I with List-II.<br/>\\(\\begin{array}{|l|l|l|l|} \\hline & \\text{List - I} & & \\text{List - II} \\\\ \\hline \\text { (A) } & \\text { Isobaric } & \\text { (I) } & \\Delta Q=\\Delta W \\\\ \\hline \\text { (B) } & \\text { Isochoric } & \\text { (II) } & \\Delta Q=\\Delta U \\\\ \\hline \\text { (C) } & \\text { Adiabatic } & \\text { (III) } & \\Delta Q=\\text { zero } \\\\ \\hline \\text { (D) } & \\text { Isothermal } & \\text { (IV) } & \\Delta Q=\\Delta U+P \\Delta V \\\\ \\hline \\end{array}\\)<br/>$\\Delta \\mathrm{Q}=$ Heat supplied<br/>$\\Delta \\mathrm{W}=$ Work done by the system<br/>$\\Delta \\mathrm{U}=$ Change in internal energy<br/>$\\mathrm{P}=$ Pressure of the system<br/>$\\Delta \\mathrm{V}=$ Change in volume of the system<br/>Choose the correct answer from the options given below:"}, "options": [{"id": "bc5d7a", "text": "(A)-(IV), (B)-(III), (C)-(II), (D)-(I)", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f142ee0e063d92350a1"}, {"id": "2bd2e6", "text": "(A)-(IV), (B)-(I), (C)-(III), (D)-(II)", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f142ee0e063d92350a2"}, {"id": "44f182", "text": "(A)-(IV), (B)-(II), (C)-(III), (D)-(I)", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f142ee0e063d92350a3"}, {"id": "b1dd18", "text": "(A)-(II), (B)-(IV), (C)-(III), (D)-(I)", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f142ee0e063d92350a4"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f142ee0e063d92350a5", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60e08408faa0944a2c3d490b"], "topics": ["60c9e88cea076dc381c0e121"], "concepts": ["60c9e88bea076dc381c0e0f1"], "question": {"text": "For the given cyclic process <math><mi>C</mi><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi></math> as shown for a gas, the work done is:<br /><br /><img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2Fltovredjtcxncsznybroozsgnsindnggwvprafyydwzlnsashv.png?alt=media\" />"}, "options": [{"id": "0e3f14", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>10</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f142ee0e063d92350a6"}, {"id": "082e38", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f142ee0e063d92350a7"}, {"id": "4391c5", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f142ee0e063d92350a8"}, {"id": "866e88", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>30</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f142ee0e063d92350a9"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f142ee0e063d92350aa", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60e08408faa0944a2c3d490b"], "topics": ["60c9e88cea076dc381c0e121"], "concepts": ["6117bc0067dbe2603c3ec296"], "question": {"text": "<p>For three low density gases <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>B</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>C</mi></math> pressure versus temperature graphs are plotted while keeping them at constant volume, as shown in the figure</p><p><img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2F50ad71df-1295-4531-9fa8-356adf8a6b98-9896704.png?alt=media\" style=\"width: 350px; height: 179px;\" /></p><p>The temperature corresponding to the point <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#39;</mo><mi>K</mi><mo>&#39;</mo></math> is:</p>"}, "options": [{"id": "4e5ae5", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>-</mo><mn>273</mn><mo>&#176;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f142ee0e063d92350ab"}, {"id": "1724ec", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>-</mo><mn>100</mn><mo>&#176;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f142ee0e063d92350ac"}, {"id": "fc874c", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8211;</mo><mn>373</mn><mo>&#176;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f142ee0e063d92350ad"}, {"id": "5dff46", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>-</mo><mn>40</mn><mo>&#176;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f142ee0e063d92350ae"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f142ee0e063d92350af", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60e08408faa0944a2c3d490b"], "topics": ["60c9e88cea076dc381c0e121"], "concepts": ["60e567ab499d1e49588f95c7"], "question": {"text": "One mole of an ideal gas passes through a process where pressure and volume obey the relation <math><mi>&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">o</mi></mrow></msub><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\" separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac><msup><mrow><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mfrac><mrow><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">o</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mfenced></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mfenced></math> . Here <math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">o</mi></mrow></msub></math> and <math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">o</mi></mrow></msub></math> are constants. Calculate the change in the temperature of the gas if its volume changes from <math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">o</mi></mrow></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi></math> to <math><mi>&#160;</mi><mn>2</mn><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">o</mi></mrow></msub></math> ."}, "options": [{"id": "377b38", "text": "<math><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfrac><mfrac><mrow><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi></mrow></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f142ee0e063d92350b0"}, {"id": "31dc98", "text": "<math><mfrac><mrow><mn>5</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfrac><mfrac><mrow><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi></mrow></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f142ee0e063d92350b1"}, {"id": "0bdbbf", "text": "<math><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac><mfrac><mrow><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi></mrow></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f142ee0e063d92350b2"}, {"id": "d840ec", "text": "<math><mfrac><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfrac><mfrac><mrow><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi></mrow></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f142ee0e063d92350b3"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f142ee0e063d92350b4", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60e08408faa0944a2c3d490b"], "topics": ["60c9e88cea076dc381c0e121"], "concepts": ["60e2fb5666f9ce3f243b4f09"], "question": {"text": "A litre of dry air at STP expands adiabatically to a volume of <math><mn>3</mn></math> litres. If <math><mi>&#947;</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1.40</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"></mi></math> the work done by air is: <math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><msup><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>1.4</mn></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>4.6555</mn></mrow></mfenced></math> [Take air to be an ideal gas]"}, "options": [{"id": "fadac8", "text": "<math><mn>60.7</mn><mi></mi><mi>J</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f142ee0e063d92350b5"}, {"id": "792b4c", "text": "<math><mn>90.5</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"></mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f142ee0e063d92350b6"}, {"id": "932bf3", "text": "<math><mn>100.8</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"></mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f142ee0e063d92350b7"}, {"id": "e42feb", "text": "<math><mn>48</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"></mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f142ee0e063d92350b8"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f142ee0e063d92350b9", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60e08408faa0944a2c3d490b"], "topics": ["60c9e88cea076dc381c0e121"], "concepts": ["60c9e88bea076dc381c0e0f1"], "question": {"text": "The heat absorbed by a system in going through the given cyclic process is :\n<img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2Frk_cil8WOBoaFAiS50kFTB3VWKXhqorLZFbmn_cAGWs.original.fullsize.png?alt=media\"><br>"}, "options": [{"id": "11a0d7", "text": "$19.6 \\mathrm{~J}$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f142ee0e063d92350ba"}, {"id": "4947af", "text": "$61.6 \\mathrm{~J}$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f142ee0e063d92350bb"}, {"id": "fe2d4e", "text": "$616 \\mathrm{~J}$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f142ee0e063d92350bc"}, {"id": "ccc04e", "text": "$431.2 \\mathrm{~J}$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f142ee0e063d92350bd"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f142ee0e063d92350be", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60e08408faa0944a2c3d490b"], "topics": ["60c9e88cea076dc381c0e121"], "concepts": ["60e567ab499d1e49588f95c7"], "question": {"text": "A vertical closed cylinder is separated into two parts by a frictionless piston of mass <math><mi>m</mi></math> and of negligible thickness. The piston is free to move along the length of the cylinder. The length of the cylinder above piston is <math><msub><mrow><mi>l</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo></math> and that below the piston is <math><msub><mrow><mi>l</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo></math> such that <math><msub><mrow><mi>l</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><msub><mrow><mi>l</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo>.</mo></math> Each part of the cylinder contains <math><mi>n</mi></math> moles of an ideal gas at equal temperature <math><mi>T</mi><mo>.</mo></math> If the piston is stationary, its mass&nbsp;<math><mi>m</mi></math>&nbsp;will be given by:<br /><br>(<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi></math> is universal gas constant and <math><mi>g</mi></math> is the acceleration due to gravity)"}, "options": [{"id": "1b0965", "text": "<math><mfrac><mrow><mi>R</mi><mi>T</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mi>g</mi></mrow></mfrac><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\" separators=\"|\"><mrow><mfrac><mrow><msub><mrow><mi>l</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn><msub><mrow><mi>l</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mi>l</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><msub><mrow><mi>l</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mfenced></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f142ee0e063d92350bf"}, {"id": "f1a5dd", "text": "<math><mfrac><mrow><mi>n</mi><mi>R</mi><mi>T</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>g</mi></mrow></mfrac><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\" separators=\"|\"><mrow><mfrac><mrow><msub><mrow><mi>l</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>-</mo><msub><mrow><mi>l</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mi>l</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><msub><mrow><mi>l</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mfenced></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f142ee0e063d92350c0"}, {"id": "64c0e6", "text": "<math><mfrac><mrow><mi>n</mi><mi>R</mi><mi>T</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>g</mi></mrow></mfrac><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\" separators=\"|\"><mrow><mfrac><mrow><msub><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mi>l</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mi>l</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mfenced></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f142ee0e063d92350c1"}, {"id": "2ad56e", "text": "<math><mfrac><mrow><mi>R</mi><mi>T</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>g</mi><mi>l</mi></mrow></mfrac><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\" separators=\"|\"><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><msub><mrow><mi>l</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mrow><mi>l</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mi>l</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><msub><mrow><mi>l</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mfenced></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f142ee0e063d92350c2"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f142ee0e063d92350c3", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60e08408faa0944a2c3d490b"], "topics": ["60c9e88cea076dc381c0e121"], "concepts": ["60e2fb5666f9ce3f243b4f09"], "question": {"text": "<p>The <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>V</mi></math> diagram of a diatomic ideal gas system going under cyclic process as shown in figure. The work done during an adiabatic process <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>C</mi><mi>D</mi></math> is (use <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#947;</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>)</mo></math> :</p><p><img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2F7a059d70-f1b4-4183-b5a3-c6bc8f12851f-image.png?alt=media\" style=\"width: 280px; height: 254px;\" /></p>"}, "options": [{"id": "53f59b", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8211;</mo><mn>500</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f142ee0e063d92350c4"}, {"id": "b17384", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8211;</mo><mn>400</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f142ee0e063d92350c5"}, {"id": "2f4334", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>400</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f142ee0e063d92350c6"}, {"id": "9b973c", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>200</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f142ee0e063d92350c7"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f142ee0e063d92350c8", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60e08408faa0944a2c3d490b"], "topics": ["60c9e88cea076dc381c0e121"], "concepts": ["60c9e88bea076dc381c0e0f1"], "question": {"text": "<p>A thermodynamic system is taken from an original state <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>D</mi></math> to an intermediate state <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>E</mi></math> by the linear process shown in the figure. Its volume is then reduced to the original volume from <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>E</mi></math> to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>F</mi></math> by an isobaric process. The total work done by the gas from <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>D</mi></math> to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>E</mi></math> to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>F</mi></math> will be</p><p><img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2F6e88af83-8b52-4a85-9bef-1f8089e65a6e-image.png?alt=media\" style=\"width: 240px; height: 195px;\" /></p>"}, "options": [{"id": "325fd9", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>-</mo><mn>450</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f142ee0e063d92350c9"}, {"id": "f5cd61", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>450</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f142ee0e063d92350ca"}, {"id": "6de68c", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>900</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f142ee0e063d92350cb"}, {"id": "62e46d", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1350</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f142ee0e063d92350cc"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f142ee0e063d92350cd", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60e08408faa0944a2c3d490b"], "topics": ["60c9e88cea076dc381c0e121"], "concepts": ["60e2fb5666f9ce3f243b4f09"], "question": {"text": "Under an adiabatic process, the volume of an ideal gas gets doubled. Consequently, the mean collision time between the gas molecule changes from <math><msub><mrow><mi>&#964;</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></math> to <math><msub><mrow><mi>&#964;</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></math> . If <math><mfrac><mrow><msub><mrow><mi>C</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>P</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mi>C</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>v</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mi>&#947;</mi></math> for this gas then a good estimate for <math><mfrac><mrow><msub><mrow><mi>&#964;</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mi>&#964;</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac></math> is given by"}, "options": [{"id": "34a3e6", "text": "<math><mn>2</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f142ee0e063d92350ce"}, {"id": "eecf6b", "text": "<math><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f142ee0e063d92350cf"}, {"id": "15c7fd", "text": "<math><msup><mrow><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mfenced></mrow><mrow><mi>γ</mi></mrow></msup></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f142ee0e063d92350d0"}, {"id": "5dd633", "text": "<math><msup><mrow><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mfenced></mrow><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow></msup></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f142ee0e063d92350d1"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f142ee0e063d92350d2", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60e08408faa0944a2c3d490b"], "topics": ["60c9e88cea076dc381c0e121"], "concepts": ["60c9e88bea076dc381c0e0f1"], "question": {"text": "The thermodynamic process, in which internal energy of the system remains constant is"}, "options": [{"id": "997dd1", "text": "Isochoric", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f142ee0e063d92350d3"}, {"id": "326a7e", "text": "Adiabatic", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f142ee0e063d92350d4"}, {"id": "84f299", "text": "Isothermal", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f142ee0e063d92350d5"}, {"id": "17c75f", "text": "Isobaric", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f142ee0e063d92350d6"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f142ee0e063d92350d7", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60e08408faa0944a2c3d490b"], "topics": ["60c9e88cea076dc381c0e121"], "concepts": ["60e2fb5666f9ce3f243b4f09"], "question": {"text": "Given below are two statements. One is labelled as Assertion (A) and the other is labelled as Reason (R).\n\nAssertion (A) : With the increase in the pressure of an ideal gas, the volume falls off more rapidly in an isothermal process in comparison to the adiabatic process.\n\nReason (R) : In isothermal process, $\\mathrm{PV}=$ constant, while in adiabatic process $\\mathrm{PV}^\\gamma=$ constant. Here $\\gamma$ is the ratio of specific heats, P is the pressure and V is the volume of the ideal gas.\n\nIn the light of the above statements, choose the correct answer from the options given below :"}, "options": [{"id": "5efa5e", "text": "Both (A) and (R) are true and (R) is the correct explanation of (A)", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f142ee0e063d92350d8"}, {"id": "c09b82", "text": "Both (A) and (R) are true but (R) is NOT the correct explanation of (A)", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f142ee0e063d92350d9"}, {"id": "825cfb", "text": "(A) is true but (R) is false", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f142ee0e063d92350da"}, {"id": "7798bd", "text": "(A) is false but (R) is true", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f142ee0e063d92350db"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f142ee0e063d92350dc", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60e08408faa0944a2c3d490b"], "topics": ["60c9e88cea076dc381c0e121"], "concepts": ["60e2fb5666f9ce3f243b4f09"], "question": {"text": "A sample of gas at temperature $T$ is adiabatically expanded to double its volume. Adiabatic constant for the gas is $\\gamma=3 / 2$. The work done by the gas in the process is:\n$(\\mu=1 \\mathrm{~mole})$"}, "options": [{"id": "013e14", "text": "$R T[1-2 \\sqrt{2}]$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f142ee0e063d92350dd"}, {"id": "01b3f9", "text": "$R T[\\sqrt{2}-2]$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f142ee0e063d92350de"}, {"id": "8a91ca", "text": "$R T[2-\\sqrt{2}]$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f142ee0e063d92350df"}, {"id": "015b47", "text": "$R T[2 \\sqrt{2}-1]$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f142ee0e063d92350e0"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f142ee0e063d92350e1", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60e08408faa0944a2c3d490b"], "topics": ["60c9e88cea076dc381c0e121"], "concepts": ["60e2fb5666f9ce3f243b4f09"], "question": {"text": "One mole of an ideal gas is taken through an adiabatic process where the temperature rises from <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>27</mn><mo>&#176;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math> to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>37</mn><mo>&#176;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math>. If the ideal gas is composed of polyatomic molecule that has 4 vibrational modes, which of the following is true? <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced open=\"[\" close=\"]\"><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>314</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi><msup><mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>mol</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">k</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mfenced></math>"}, "options": [{"id": "54bec8", "text": "work done by the gas is close to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>332</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f142ee0e063d92350e2"}, {"id": "c9e613", "text": "work done on the gas is close to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>582</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f142ee0e063d92350e3"}, {"id": "2763b7", "text": "work done by the gas is close to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>582</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f142ee0e063d92350e4"}, {"id": "7c73c8", "text": "work done on the gas is close to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>332</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f142ee0e063d92350e5"}], "questionLabels": []}], "markingScheme": {"_id": "608283e223cf4b3ad8f125e6", "title": "JEE Single Correct", "correctAttempt": 4, "incorrectAttempt": -1, "createdAt": "2021-04-09T08:45:27.797Z", "updatedAt": "2021-07-05T05:39:15.785Z", "__v": 0, "updated_by": "6042252509c5bf34e8a2f178"}, "maximumAttemptLimit": 20, "linkedQuestions": [], "createdAt": "2026-04-14T14:28:36.106Z", "updatedAt": "2026-04-14T14:28:36.106Z", "__v": 0}, "position": 0, "_id": "69de4f142ee0e063d9235135"}, {"sectionId": {"_id": "69de4f142ee0e063d9235130", "title": "Physics Numerical", "sectionType": "normal", "subject": "607018ee404ae53194e73d90", "questions": [{"_id": "69de4f142ee0e063d923510f", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60e08408faa0944a2c3d490b"], "topics": ["60e0877ad7588a2678f93bc6"], "concepts": ["6117b8e067dbe2603c3e8a74"], "question": {"text": "The total internal energy of two mole monoatomic ideal gas at temperature <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>T</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>300</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi></math> will be _____&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi></math>. (Given <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>31</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi>mol</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#183;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi></math>)"}, "options": [{"id": "af5a74", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f142ee0e063d9235110"}, {"id": "c8bd96", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f142ee0e063d9235111"}, {"id": "79eca6", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f142ee0e063d9235112"}, {"id": "0ce159", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f142ee0e063d9235113"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f142ee0e063d9235114", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60e08408faa0944a2c3d490b"], "topics": ["60c9e88cea076dc381c0e121"], "concepts": ["60e2fb5666f9ce3f243b4f09"], "question": {"text": "An ideal gas initially at $0^{\\circ} \\mathrm{C}$ temperature, is compressed suddenly to one fourth of its volume. If the ratio of specific heat at constant pressure to that at constant volume is $3 / 2$, the change in temperature due to the thermodynamic process is _____ K."}, "options": [{"id": "a0b6a6", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f142ee0e063d9235115"}, {"id": "59d15d", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f142ee0e063d9235116"}, {"id": "11bc1e", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f142ee0e063d9235117"}, {"id": "8ac3d2", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f142ee0e063d9235118"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f142ee0e063d9235119", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60e08408faa0944a2c3d490b"], "topics": ["60e0877ad7588a2678f93bc6"], "concepts": ["60e2fad966f9ce3f243b4739"], "question": {"text": "In a certain thermodynamical process, the pressure of a gas depends on its volume as <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>k</mi><msup><mi>V</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></math>. The work done when the temperature changes from <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>100</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#176;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math> to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>300</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#176;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math> will be <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mi>n</mi><mi>R</mi></math>&nbsp;where <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>n</mi></math> denotes number of moles of a gas find&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi></math>&nbsp;;"}, "options": [{"id": "df6cfb", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f142ee0e063d923511a"}, {"id": "72f47d", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f142ee0e063d923511b"}, {"id": "a6d735", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f142ee0e063d923511c"}, {"id": "d345fd", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f142ee0e063d923511d"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f142ee0e063d923511e", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60e08408faa0944a2c3d490b"], "topics": ["60c9e88cea076dc381c0e121"], "concepts": ["60e2fb5666f9ce3f243b4f09"], "question": {"text": "Starting at temperature <math><mn>300</mn><mi></mi><mi>K</mi><mo>,</mo></math> one mole of an ideal diatomic gas <math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>&#947;</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1.4</mn></mrow></mfenced></math> is first compressed adiabatically from volume <math><msub><mrow><mi>V</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></math> to <math><msub><mrow><mi>V</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mrow><mi>V</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mrow><mn>16</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>.</mo></math> It is then allowed to expand isobarically to volume <math><mn>2</mn><msub><mrow><mi>V</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></math> . If all the processes are the quasi-static then the final temperature of the gas (in <math><msup><mrow><mi></mi></mrow><mrow><mi>o</mi></mrow></msup><mi>K</mi></math> ) is (to the nearest integer) ___________."}, "options": [{"id": "68625b", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f142ee0e063d923511f"}, {"id": "18de88", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f142ee0e063d9235120"}, {"id": "2bde2a", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f142ee0e063d9235121"}, {"id": "009038", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f142ee0e063d9235122"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f142ee0e063d9235123", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60e08408faa0944a2c3d490b"], "topics": ["60e0877ad7588a2678f93bc6"], "concepts": ["60e08778d7588a2678f93ba3"], "question": {"text": "The volume&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>V</mi></math> of a given mass of monoatomic gas changes with temperature&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>T</mi></math> according to the relation <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>V</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>K</mi><msup><mi>T</mi><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac></msup></math>. The workdone when temperature changes by&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>90</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi></math>&nbsp;will be <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mi>R</mi></math>. The value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi></math>&nbsp;is<br />[<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi></math>&nbsp;universal gas constant ]"}, "options": [{"id": "b90d30", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f142ee0e063d9235124"}, {"id": "ff7b57", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f142ee0e063d9235125"}, {"id": "df0610", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f142ee0e063d9235126"}, {"id": "a76268", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f142ee0e063d9235127"}], "questionLabels": []}], "markingScheme": {"_id": "608283c623cf4b3ad8f125e5", "title": "JEE Numerical", "correctAttempt": 4, "incorrectAttempt": -1, "createdAt": "2021-04-09T08:45:27.797Z", "updatedAt": "2021-07-05T05:39:27.056Z", "__v": 0, "updated_by": "6042252509c5bf34e8a2f178"}, "maximumAttemptLimit": 5, "linkedQuestions": [], "createdAt": "2026-04-14T14:28:36.200Z", "updatedAt": "2026-04-14T14:28:36.200Z", "__v": 0}, "position": 1, "_id": "69de4f142ee0e063d9235136"}], "bonusSections": [], "packDetails": [], "p